    {"page":18,"para":1,"sent":0,"ok":true,"text":"The board is the parameter plane and you tilt it: W A S D (or ← →) pitch and roll the valley under the white ball."}
    {"page":18,"para":2,"sent":0,"ok":true,"text":"The c slider is the damping coefficient — β’s role, made physical."}
    {"page":19,"para":1,"sent":0,"ok":true,"text":"Level 2 is Rosenbrock: a strongly curved valley whose floor is nearly flat, with the minimum around the bend."}
    {"page":20,"para":1,"sent":0,"ok":true,"text":"You reached the scorecard without playing, so the white ghost is a guided demo ride — a hand-steered route through Rosenbrock’s valley, not yours."}
    {"page":21,"para":1,"sent":1,"ok":true,"text":"One hundred balls are scattered across whichever country you picked and released; each runs the same physics you just played — no tilt, mid-range damping — and settles into the first basin its trajectory enters."}
    {"page":21,"para":2,"sent":2,"ok":true,"text":"The panel’s scorecard keeps each cluster’s count and mean final loss — the same landscape, the same rule, and a different answer from every starting point."}
    {"page":21,"para":3,"sent":0,"ok":true,"text":"ensembles (many restarts) cover ground faster — together the hundred balls paint roughly 20× the ground any one of them crosses alone — but no ball ever sees the whole map: the ensemble’s information exceeds any member’s — and where a ball lands is a property of its basin, not of how hard it tried"}
